= Cryptography — Simple =

'''Cryptography''' uses mathematics to protect information and communications against attackers.

Encryption is one part of cryptography.

Cryptography also includes digital signatures, message authentication, secure key exchange, hashing, and other techniques.

Encryption hides information so authorized parties can recover it.

A cryptographic hash is different: it produces a digest and is not meant to be reversed like encryption.

Good cryptography still needs correct software, safe keys, good randomness, and secure system design.

